Ladybird’s URL filters match as Firefox’s MatchURLFilters.sys.mjs does:
hostContains tests the host with a dot in front, a query is compared
without its question mark, Contains, Prefix, and Suffix never match
an empty part, urlMatches runs on the URL without its fragment and
originAndPathMatches without its query too, and a URL with no port uses
its scheme’s default. Chromium’s URLMatcher (components/url_matcher)
has the same key set and the same implicit dot for hostContains. Error
messages use Firefox’s schema wording, which extensions may compare.
